Enterprise identity | SSO/SCIM grouped tag: 3 mentions; underlying matches are SSO. | Integrate customer SSO and test permission changes. The data does not establish three SCIM requirements.

Transformer and classical ML foundations

The workbook does not establish broad demand for a large transformer-theory or classical-ML module. PyTorch appears in five descriptions, four role-linked. The single Hugging Face/Transformers match is not proof of a transformer-architecture requirement. Classical ML algorithms are not separately measured.

Include concise foundations where they support model selection, evaluation and adaptation. Justify that content as prerequisite knowledge. Reserve deeper training and serving material for relevant specialisations rather than presenting it as a universal market requirement.

Where to incorporate the changes

Add reuse and customer product feedback to milestone reviews and the final handover. Add a complete experiment to model adaptation, context and memory to agents, and an alternate-cloud exercise to deployment. Use the new-client capstone to test unfamiliar-stack integration and independent operation.

Prioritise reusable solutions, product feedback, model adaptation and assessed production delivery first. Cloud, platform and inference options can vary by learner target role. Reallocate existing class time or replace optional exercises before committing to additional required content.

